FORMAT 1
SCENARIO A shared cookbook in pairs
LABEL    Worksheet 4
SUMMARY  Anna and Petr: a shared repository, an invitation, cloning, a rejected push and pull.
INTRO    You play both: **Anna** (owns the repository) and **Petr** (collaborator). Switch between their computers and GitHub with the tabs at the top.

SETUP
  PERSON anna NAME "Anna Svobodová" EMAIL "svobodovaa@jirovcovka.net" LOGIN "anna-svobodova" LABEL "Anna's computer"
  PERSON petr NAME "Petr Dvořák" EMAIL "dvorakp@jirovcovka.net" LOGIN "petr-dvorak" LABEL "Petr's computer"
  MACHINE anna CONFIGURED
  MACHINE petr CONFIGURED
  SHOW GITHUB
  REPOSITORY git/shared-cookbook
  AS anna
  PS> mkdir git
  PS> cd git
  AS petr
  PS> mkdir git
  PS> cd git
END

TASK **Anna** creates a repository **shared-cookbook** on GitHub: Private, and she **ticks** Add a README file.
  NOTE  Switch to **GitHub (Anna)** → New → name, Private, tick **Add a README file** → Create repository.
  CHECK github anna-svobodova/shared-cookbook has branch main
END

TASK **Anna** invites Petr: Settings → Collaborators → Add people → **petr-dvorak**. **Petr** accepts the invitation.
  NOTE  Petr sees the invitation at the top of GitHub (tab **GitHub (Petr)**).
  CHECK github anna-svobodova/shared-cookbook has collaborator petr-dvorak
END

TASK Both clone the repository into the **git** folder and open it in VS Code.
  NOTE  Copy the address on GitHub (**Copy**) and paste it in the terminal with **Ctrl+V**.
  HINT  git clone https://github.com/anna-svobodova/shared-cookbook.git
  HINT  cd shared-cookbook
  HINT  code -r .
  CHECK anna: repository exists
  CHECK petr: repository exists
END

TASK Each of them creates a **different** recipe (just a heading is enough) and commits it. **Anna** pushes first, **then** Petr.
  HINT     git add .
  HINT     git commit -m "Add potato soup"
  HINT     git push
  QUESTION What happened when Petr pushed?
  CHECK    petr: output of "git push..." contains "[rejected]"
END

TASK **Petr** fixes it as the hint suggests: he pulls and pushes again. **Anna** then pulls Petr's recipe.
  NOTE  Petr:
  HINT  git pull
  HINT  git push
  NOTE  Anna:
  HINT  git pull
  CHECK anna: github anna-svobodova/shared-cookbook main equals HEAD
  CHECK petr: github anna-svobodova/shared-cookbook main equals HEAD
  CHECK github anna-svobodova/shared-cookbook main is a merge
END

TASK **Anna** adds a quote (`>`) to the README, commits and pushes. **Petr** pulls.
  HINT     > A cookbook we write together.
  QUESTION Which two commands start and end your work on a shared project?
  CHECK    file README.md on github anna-svobodova/shared-cookbook contains line starting with ">"
  CHECK    petr: github anna-svobodova/shared-cookbook main equals HEAD
END
